        "title": "Zero pair support can prevent universal unbiased variance estimation",
        "statement": "For two units sampled one at a time, shows pi_12=0, the all-pairs inverse expression cannot use that unsupported pair, the supported-pair truncation is biased, and no estimator based on the observed singleton can be unbiased for the HT variance for every finite population.",
        "strategy": "Write the two-point design and its variance explicitly; use a four-value rectangle identity to contradict the form of every observed-record estimator.",
